<pr_description>
IOFS.ReadDir should check for fs.ReadDirFile

New interfaces introduced:
Method: BasePathFile.ReadDir(n int) ([]fs.DirEntry, error)
Location: basepath.go (type *BasePathFile)
Inputs: n int – maximum number of directory entries to return (use -1 to read all). The method is called via the fs.ReadDirFile interface on a file opened from a BasePathFs.
Outputs: slice of fs.DirEntry representing the directory entries and an error (if the underlying read fails). When the wrapped file implements fs.ReadDirFile the call is delegated; otherwise a fallback using readDirFile is used.
Description: Added to make *BasePathFile conform to the fs.ReadDirFile interface, allowing native DirEntry objects to be retrieved directly from a base‑path‑restricted file system.

Method: IOFS.ReadDir(name string) ([]fs.DirEntry, error)
Location: iofs.go (type IOFS)
Inputs: name string – path of the directory to read.
Outputs: slice of fs.DirEntry and an error. The implementation now opens the directory, checks if the returned file implements fs.ReadDirFile and, if so, uses its ReadDir method; otherwise it falls back to Readdir and sorts the results.
Description: Updated to prefer the native fs.ReadDirFile interface when available, enabling fs.WalkDir to receive native DirEntry objects from an IOFS wrapping a BasePathFs.

</pr_description>

